WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.040
Scientists have measured carbon dioxide in the air on a Hawaiian volcano since 1958.

2
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.540
Each year it rises through winter and spring, then falls through summer.

3
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.920
The whole record slowly climbs.

4
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.600
Why? In Virginia, an oak pulls water from the soil.

5
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.560
That water leaves as an invisible gas.

6
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.340
Where do the carbon and the water go next?

7
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.000
Carbon is in the sugar, fat and protein of every living thing.

8
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.240
The carbon cycle is carbon moving among air, living things, ocean and soil.

9
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.980
Photosynthesis takes carbon dioxide out of the air.

10
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.640
Plants, algae and some bacteria use radiant energy to make sugar, called glucose,

11
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.800
from carbon dioxide and water.

12
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.850
Three processes return carbon.

13
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.630
Respiration is cells breaking down sugar and releasing carbon dioxide and water.

14
00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.550
Plants, animals and decomposers do it, day and night.

15
00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.570
Decomposition is bacteria and fungi breaking down dead organisms and returning

16
00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.070
carbon to air and soil.

17
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.070
Combustion is burning.

18
00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.790
Burning coal, oil or natural gas releases carbon dioxide quickly.

19
00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:17.533
Water has its own cycle.

20
00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:22.213
Evaporation is liquid water changing into water vapor, a gas.

21
00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:26.793
Condensation is vapor cooling into droplets that form clouds.

22
00:01:27.813 --> 00:01:30.633
Precipitation is water falling as rain or snow.

23
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:34.153
Infiltration is water soaking into the ground.

24
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.553
Runoff is water flowing over land into streams.

25
00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:41.953
Transpiration is plants releasing water vapor from their leaves.

26
00:01:41.953 --> 00:01:42.953
Subs by www .zeoranger .co .uk

27
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:45.497
The two cycles meet inside living things.

28
00:01:46.437 --> 00:01:49.637
Photosynthesis uses water and carbon dioxide together.

29
00:01:50.637 --> 00:01:53.937
In a dry summer, plants close the tiny openings in their leaves.

30
00:01:54.797 --> 00:01:57.817
That saves water, but less carbon dioxide gets in.

31
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.857
A change in one cycle can change the other.

32
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.040
Back to the volcano.

33
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.520
Most land plants are in the Northern Hemisphere.

34
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.880
Each northern spring, leaves grow and photosynthesis speeds up.

35
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.680
Each fall, photosynthesis slows and many trees drop their leaves, but respiration

36
00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.540
and decomposition keep going.

37
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.120
Air at Mauna Loa mixes with air from across the north.

38
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.040
So carbon dioxide falls each northern summer and rises each winter.

39
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.600
Underneath, the record climbs, mostly from burning fossil fuels.
